Executive Summary
Currently, lab technicians perform weekly instrument checks and save the results to a shared folder. Lab managers then manually review the data for trends 
and out-of-control (OOC) conditions. With multiple instruments and competing priorities, reviews can be delayed or missed, increasing the risk of undetected 
instrument issues, compliance concerns, and unreliable data.

The proposed solution uses Power BI and Power Automate to automatically analyze weekly instrument data, identify potential trend or OOC conditions, and 
immediately notify the appropriate lab personnel. Generative AI can then provide a standardized summary of the detected issue and potential next steps, 
while technicians remain responsible for validating the data and determining corrective action.

The opportunity is to reduce manual review effort, improve the speed and consistency of OOC detection, strengthen auditability, and reduce the risk
associated with missed reviews. A small, controlled prototype should be conducted to determine whether the automated approach provides measurable 
improvements over the current manual process.
